\caption{From image cues to a regional measurement. (a) Conceptual chain: correspondence is inferred and strain depends on the measurement definition. The registration objective is an example, not a universal loss. Segment~11 is reduced; all curve readouts are calculated illustrations. Input (I), estimation (E) and representation (R) tests probe potentially coupled errors. (b) Selected empirical endpoints, not a pooled ranking. MRXCAT2.0 reports slice averages~\cite{mrxcat2023}. Militaru LS/CS ICCs compare FT with tagging; its RS range compares FT vendors~\cite{militaru2021}. Cao reports mid-slice peak Ecc~\cite{cao2018}; StrainNet reports end-systolic cine--DENSE Ecc agreement~\cite{wang2023strainnet}. REGAIN assesses reconstruction-plus-analysis agreement~\cite{yoon2023regain}; Strain-8 assesses repeatability~\cite{bell2025strain8}. Kihlberg's ROC uses end-systolic segmental Ecc and LGE~\cite{kihlberg2020clinical}. Bello's corrected C index concerns RV survival prediction in pulmonary hypertension~\cite{bello2019}; DLSS AUC evaluates reader-defined wall-motion abnormality across thresholds~\cite{masutani2023dlss}. The axis value 0.5 is a scale reference, not an observed result. Code revision used OpenAI Codex 0.162.1 (GPT-6 Astra); see declarations.}
Deep-learning aligned strain also separates motion estimation from clinical classification. Its cine pipeline detects key phases, segments the myocardium and estimates deformation using image similarity, smoothness and mask agreement; LGE labels the downstream patient-level fibrosis classifier, not the displacement field. Development used 57 patients with Duchenne muscular dystrophy, followed by a same-centre temporal holdout of 82 patients. The classification target was the presence of at least one LGE-positive segment, rather than the spatial boundary of fibrosis~\cite{koehler2025alignedstrain}. In a different chamber and population, Bello and colleagues used right-ventricular motion to predict survival in 302 patients with pulmonary hypertension. Internally bootstrap-corrected Harrell C indices were 0.75 for the learned model and 0.59 for a model using manually measured conventional volumetric and functional variables~\cite{bello2019}. Both studies provide clinically relevant discrimination evidence in their tested settings, without converting that evidence into dense motion accuracy or demonstrated treatment benefit.
Survival-supervised motion & 2019; Nat Mach Intell~\cite{bello2019} & RV cine-derived motion; supervised on survival in pulmonary hypertension & Learned low-dimensional motion representation & 302 patients; internally bootstrap-corrected Harrell C 0.75 (95\% CI 0.70--0.79) versus conventional manual-variable model 0.59 (0.53--0.65) & Prognostic discrimination in PH; not an LV focal-motion or management-impact endpoint \\

\caption{From image cues to a regional measurement. (a) Conceptual chain: correspondence is inferred and strain depends on the measurement definition. The registration objective is an example, not a universal loss. Segment~11 is reduced; all curve readouts are calculated illustrations. Input (I), estimation (E) and representation (R) tests probe potentially coupled errors. (b) Selected empirical endpoints, not a pooled ranking. MRXCAT2.0 reports slice averages~\cite{mrxcat2023}. Militaru LS/CS ICCs compare FT with tagging; its RS range compares FT vendors~\cite{militaru2021}. Cao reports mid-slice peak Ecc~\cite{cao2018}; StrainNet reports end-systolic cine--DENSE Ecc agreement~\cite{wang2023strainnet}. REGAIN assesses reconstruction-plus-analysis agreement~\cite{yoon2023regain}; Strain-8 assesses repeatability~\cite{bell2025strain8}. Kihlberg's ROC uses end-systolic segmental Ecc and LGE~\cite{kihlberg2020clinical}. Bello's corrected C index concerns RV survival prediction in pulmonary hypertension~\cite{bello2019}; DLSS AUC evaluates reader-defined wall-motion abnormality across thresholds~\cite{masutani2023dlss}. The axis value 0.5 is a scale reference, not an observed result. Code revision used OpenAI Codex 0.162.1 (GPT-6 Astra); see declarations.}
Clinical labels enter these pipelines at different stages. Cine-only infarct delineation combines recurrent motion features and optical flow with manual delayed-enhancement delineations as the target~\cite{xu2018}. DLSS predicts myocardial velocities and segmentation, using velocity supervision from registered 4D-flow MRI and segmentation targets generated by commercial software, and derives strain from cine at inference. Its development dataset contained 223 examinations from 219 patients; four-reader consensus wall-motion labels were used for the separate clinical evaluation in 53 patients and 846 segments. The ROC AUC was 0.90; a 30\% peak-radial-strain threshold gave sensitivity 86\% and specificity 85\%~\cite{masutani2023dlss}. Thus the reader labels evaluate the clinical output rather than supervise the motion network.
DL synthetic strain & 2023; Radiol Cardiothorac Imaging~\cite{masutani2023dlss} & Cine at inference; training targets: coregistered 4D-flow velocity and commercial-software segmentation & Velocity and segmentation network; strain derived from estimated motion & Development: 223 exams/219 patients; clinical test: 53 patients/846 segments, four-reader WMA consensus; ROC AUC 0.90; 30\% peak Err threshold: sensitivity 86\%, specificity 85\% & WMA clinical endpoint; reader labels evaluate the output, not the motion-training target \\

\caption{From image cues to a regional measurement. (a) Conceptual chain: correspondence is inferred and strain depends on the measurement definition. The registration objective is an example, not a universal loss. Segment~11 is reduced; all curve readouts are calculated illustrations. Input (I), estimation (E) and representation (R) tests probe potentially coupled errors. (b) Selected empirical endpoints, not a pooled ranking. MRXCAT2.0 reports slice averages~\cite{mrxcat2023}. Militaru LS/CS ICCs compare FT with tagging; its RS range compares FT vendors~\cite{militaru2021}. Cao reports mid-slice peak Ecc~\cite{cao2018}; StrainNet reports end-systolic cine--DENSE Ecc agreement~\cite{wang2023strainnet}. REGAIN assesses reconstruction-plus-analysis agreement~\cite{yoon2023regain}; Strain-8 assesses repeatability~\cite{bell2025strain8}. Kihlberg's ROC uses end-systolic segmental Ecc and LGE~\cite{kihlberg2020clinical}. Bello's corrected C index concerns RV survival prediction in pulmonary hypertension~\cite{bello2019}; DLSS AUC evaluates reader-defined wall-motion abnormality across thresholds~\cite{masutani2023dlss}. The axis value 0.5 is a scale reference, not an observed result. Code revision used OpenAI Codex 0.162.1 (GPT-6 Astra); see declarations.}
Reconstruction changes the images supplied to a downstream estimator, and primary studies show both agreement and residual bias. REGAIN was trained on 1616 patients and tested prospectively in 181 participants; its paired breath-hold comparison used 94 patients and 36 healthy participants, while global radial, circumferential and longitudinal feature-tracking strain was available in 49 participants. Mean global-strain differences versus a separately acquired GRAPPA cine were near zero, while the 95\% limits of agreement remained \(-7\%\) to 6\% for radial, \(-2\%\) to 3\% for circumferential and \(-3\%\) to 3\% for longitudinal strain~\cite{yoon2023regain}. CineVN compared prospectively accelerated acquisitions with conventional GRAPPA in 18 healthy volunteers. On individual mid-ventricular slices, CineVN had the smallest bias and narrowest limits among the tested accelerated reconstructions, yet all accelerated protocols significantly underestimated peak radial strain and overestimated peak circumferential strain; its 46-patient demonstration lacked a conventional reference and reported slice exclusions after segmentation failure~\cite{vornehm2024cinevn}. These are measured reconstruction-plus-analysis results. Whether deep learning removes or preserves a focal abnormality is a separate question that they do not address.
Accelerated reconstruction can alter temporal sharpness, noise texture and edge appearance, all of which may affect downstream motion estimation even when conventional image-quality scores remain acceptable. Primary evidence is encouraging but endpoint-specific. In REGAIN, global feature-tracking strain from 49 participants showed near-zero mean differences between separately acquired accelerated and GRAPPA breath-hold cine, with non-zero limits of agreement~\cite{yoon2023regain}. CineVN's paired 18-volunteer comparison found the smallest strain bias among the tested accelerated reconstructions, but all accelerated protocols retained systematic peak radial/circumferential bias; the 46-patient demonstration had no conventional reference and included segmentation-related slice exclusions~\cite{vornehm2024cinevn}. In ten healthy volunteers, model-based DLR reduced the dispersion of global circumferential strain differences from full sampling at high reduction factors relative to compressed sensing, while bias and radial underestimation remained~\cite{tsuneta2025dlr}. DENT improved image-phase interpolation and reader-rated temporal presentation across a large multicentre development set and prospective testing, but it did not evaluate myocardial strain or validate its deformation vectors as tissue motion~\cite{morales2024dent}. These measured findings motivate joint reconstruction--estimator tests; they neither show nor imply that deep learning erases focal abnormalities.
